# Netlify reads this from the published folder.
#
# A quiz is loaded by the shell, which lives on another origin: the browser
# fetches `remoteEntry.json` and imports the modules cross-origin, and both
# need CORS. Everything here is a public, versioned static file, so any
# origin may read it — there is nothing user-specific to protect.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
